NAME
       mkpart - create a partition table

SYNOPSIS
       mkpart [-f] <device> <type>:<size> [<type>:<size> ...]

DESCRIPTION
       Writes a fresh partition table on DEVICE with the partitions
       given. Each argument is a type and a size, and a size of 0 or
       the last entry takes the remaining space.

       This destroys the existing table, so it asks for confirmation
       unless -f is given.

OPTIONS
       -f     do not ask for confirmation

EXAMPLES
       mkpart /dev/sda fat32:512M ext4:0

SEE ALSO
       fdisk(1), mkfs(1), wipefs(1)
